{"name":"Calcareous Sinter","hex":"#ddeeff","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"calcareous","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Resembling, containing, or composed of calcium carbonate or limestone; chalky.","Growing in a chalky habitat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/calcareous"},{"term":"sinter","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An alluvial sediment deposited by a mineral spring.","A mass formed by sintering."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To heat a compacted powder mass to form a hardened mass."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sinter"}],"entries":[{"title":"Calcareous sinter","blocks":[{"text":"Calcareous sinter is a freshwater calcium carbonate deposit, also known as calc-sinter. Deposits are characterised by low porosity and well-developed lamination, often forming crusts or sedimentary rock layers. Calcareous sinter should not be confused with siliceous sinter, which the term sinter more frequently refers to. It has been suggested that the term \"sinter\" should be restricted to siliceous spring deposits and be dropped for calcareous deposits entirely."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calcareous_sinter"},{"title":"Calcareous","blocks":[{"text":"Calcareous is an adjective meaning \"mostly or partly composed of calcium carbonate\", in other words, containing lime or being chalky. The term is used in a wide variety of scientific disciplines."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Calcareous_Soil_Profile%2C_Seven_Sisters_Country_Park_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1280181.jpg/330px-Calcareous_Soil_Profile%2C_Seven_Sisters_Country_Park_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1280181.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calcareous"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Kalksinter.JPG/120px-Kalksinter.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_con